  effectList:
  - '-'
  - '-'
  - '-'
  - Slide 50% faster with highly reduced friction.
  - '-'
  - Holding shift in the air propells you forward relative to your sprint speed.
  - '-'
  - '-'
  - '-'
  - '-'
  - '-'
  - Bullets are affected by gravity.
  - '-'
  - '-'
  - Randomly rerolls your mutated items into an other mutated item. Each stack decreases
    time between rerolls and adds a chance to create items out of nowhere.
  - '-'
  - Weapon becomes a charge shot. Giving damage, bullet speed, and accuracy for charge.
    Charge speed scales with attack speed. Stacking gives a higher charge speed and
    a higher charge cap.
  - Every 20 seconds get a random buff with a 20% chance of getting a debuff instead.
    Stacking lowers debuff chance by 10% and makes buffs / debuffs from this more
    effective.
  - When damaged, let out a explosion that does damage relative to the amount of
    damage that you took. This explosion has a 15% chance to damage you, causing
    the explosion again. Stacking increases the radias and the damage.
  - Execute enemies below 5% HP. Stacking increases execution range, aproching but
    never reaching 50%.
  - Gain a stack of bunny hop when you land giving Jump Height+ Speed+ for every
    consecutive jump up to 2 + your stacks. Stacking also increases how much speed
    and jump height you get per stack.
  - Bullets have a 25% chance to do 15% of enimes current hp as damage. Stacking
    further increases the chance by 5%.
  - '-'
  - When above 80% HP, Passive healing damages you.
  - Every minute reroll a random common item into a random mutated item. On stacking
    timer shortens by 50%, and adds an increasing chace to reroll a uncommon item
    instead.
  - Fire an additional bullet when you shoot. A bullet is then also fired from where
    the first bullet hit, towards the second bullet.
  - 
  - 
  - Bullets have a 10% chance to jam enemy ranged projectile users, meaning their
    next shot will be canceled. Stacking increases odds by 5% and allows jammed to
    stack an additonal time.
  - Your pants have fallen. Reloading has you pull up your pants, giving you a deteriorating
    bonus to your speed for 5 seconds. Stacking adds 5 more seconds.
  - Your health deteriorates at a rate of 1% per second, or 3% per second when under
    33% health. Killing an enemy causes the self damage to become healing at a doubled
    rate and increases movement speed and firerate by 50% for 5 (+5 per stack) seconds.
  - '-'
  - '-'
  - Periodicly load bullets directly into your magazine. Stacks decrease time between
    loading.
  - each bullet you fire has a 5% chance of being made by FIREPOWER(tm). These enchanced
    masterwork bullets made with a love for engeneiring and a true care for the craft
    ignite the enemy for DOT.
  - 
  - 
